NUM-41: give RDII the rain that fell in each time step, not a point sample

RDIISolver recorded the gage rate at the start of each UH rain interval and,
like legacy getRainfall(), used the first one of each RDII time step for all
intervals of that step. advance() now adds every runoff substep's rain to the
RDII step it falls in (a substep never crosses a gage entry boundary) and
queues the step's average rate, merging runs of equal rate as the legacy fix
does so both give the same numbers. emitTick() gives each rain interval that
average times the part of the step it covers.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-41_swmm600.patch

